# Line endings are pinned here because nothing pinned them before, and it cost a commit.
#
# Git for Windows clones with core.autocrlf=true: the object store holds LF, the working
# tree gets CRLF. Any tool that then commits from a Linux side with autocrlf unset sees
# all 70 text files as modified and writes CRLF into the object store. That happened once
# already, turning a one-file fix into a 25,937-line diff.
#
# `text=auto` normalizes every text file to LF in the repository regardless of who commits
# it. The per-extension rules then decide what each platform gets on checkout.

* text=auto

# Scripts, where the ending is not cosmetic: a .sh with CRLF fails on Linux with
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", and PowerShell is happiest with CRLF.
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf

# Never touch these.
*.gz   binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.bundle binary
